      .partialImplementation
      "The isotropic linear category and actual base-identity linear endomorphism monoids are typed. For an arbitrary Frobenioid, Definition 1.3's pullback, co-angular pre-step, factorization, and isotropic-hull universal properties construct the contravariant monoid transport with identity and composition laws and the injective isotropic-hull map. The construction is uniquely characterized by Proposition 1.11(iv)'s commuting equation. The explicit Theorem 5.2 model transport remains available as a coordinate-level specialization. Proposition 2.2(i) and the divisor/unit/characteristic-quotient assertions of (iii) remain open.",
    clause "FrdI.2.3" .frobenioidsI
      "Frobenioids I, Definition 2.3"
      ["PreFrobenioid.CharacteristicSplitting",
        "SplitFrobenioidPresentation",
        "SplitFrobenioidEquivalence",
        "SplitFrobenioidEquivalence.refl",
        "SplitFrobenioidEquivalence.trans"]
