      "Mochizuki's official correction (29) is enforced: for an arbitrary Frobenioid presentation, the filtered Hom colimit is a connected, totally epimorphic group-like pre-Frobenioid and the canonical functor is faithful; a full Frobenioid is not claimed unconditionally. The complete C-to-F_Phi^gp-to-F_0 diagram and Proposition 4.4(iv) dictionary are generic. Under the exact Definition 4.5(i) hypothesis of birational Frobenius normalization, the corrected isotropic degree-two square-law argument proves commutativity of target rational functions, unit transport depends only on the base arrow, and every Definition 1.3 axiom is packaged as a generic Frobenioid presentation. Target rational functions have exactly the localized source units as the kernel of their Phi^gp divisor map. Their pullback-stable objectwise images descend to the generic contravariant subgroup family Phi^birat, with its restricted elementary category, faithful inclusion, base-indexed surjection, exact kernel, and rational-image uniqueness. Objectwise degree-two potentials normalize every birational arrow into Phi^birat, yielding the literal restricted factor functor and a natural isomorphism from its ambient composite to the raw groupified functor. Finally, the localization universal property supplies the canonical comparison to the earlier Theorem 5.2 filtered-colimit implementation; after the tautological Phi^gp ambient conversion, both raw divisor functors and the complete restricted-factor diagrams are naturally isomorphic.",
