      "On printed/PDF pages 9-10, a connected anabelioid is represented by an actual Mathlib Galois category, a fiber functor, and a certified profinite fundamental group. For an orbicurve, the category's objects are representably finite-etale stack maps to that exact orbicurve, its hom-sets are bijective with actual stack morphisms over the target, and its fiber functor is naturally identified with literal geometric fibers. Its unpointed morphisms are exactly contravariant functors preserving finite limits and finite colimits, with no basepoint comparison field. Exactness is proved to make the pulled-back fiber a fiber functor, and a comparison with the target fiber is then derived. The pointed specialization, its continuous fundamental-group homomorphism, closed image, identity, and composition laws are derived from automorphisms of fiber functors.",
