      "For Proposition 1.1.4 and Lemma 1.1.5 on printed/PDF pages 11-13, Lean defines HomOut(G,H) as the category of continuous homomorphisms and explicit target conjugators, defines Mor(B(G),B(H)) as exact pullbacks and natural isomorphisms, proves the arrow-level conjugator/natural-isomorphism bijection, and obtains the stated categorical equivalence. Its decategorification is the established equivalence between exact-functor isomorphism classes and continuous-homomorphism inner-conjugacy classes, preserving identities and composition. Separately, basepoint-compatible natural isomorphisms force literal equality of recovered homomorphisms, giving Proposition 1.1.4(ii)'s bijection between actual continuous homomorphisms and pointed morphism classes. The result is connected to the existing pointed categorical-equivalence and connected finite-etale open-image endpoints.",
