      .sourceFaithful
      "Lean constructs the literal connected source diagram and Definition 2.1 category B(G), including the verticial gluing and the unique isolated-edge case. In the verticial case it proves the glued category's pre-Galois and fiber-functor axioms, hence obtains its Galois-category structure. Every object produces the finite-etale semigraph G^S with proper finite-fiber projection, and every morphism produces a functorial proper refinement over G. A connected object now yields a connected semigraph by constructing the constituent subobjects selected by one semigraph component, gluing them across branches, and using categorical connectedness to show that subobject is the whole object. Pointed Galois objects form inhabited cofiltered categories cofinal among connected finite-etale objects in both the verticial and isolated-edge cases. Each level is identified with the normal-open quotient of the appropriate fiber-functor automorphism group by its point stabilizer, and its full Galois automorphism group acts on the associated semigraph, transitively on every applicable vertex and edge fiber. The isolated construction deliberately retains full constituent automorphisms even when their visible incidence action is trivial. Refinement symmetries and their equivariance are derived from unique Galois automorphism descent and are proved surjective. No connectedness, semigraph, action, subgroup, deck group, or transition homomorphism is accepted as an output-shaped field.",
