      "M_TM^x is now the range of an injective unit Kummer homomorphism, and its torsion M_TM^mu is proved exactly equal to the image of torsion units. The literal mono-analytic absolute-Galois TM-pair and coefficient-identity Kummer embedding are source-constructed, and their full monoid and unit maps reduce definitionally to the compatible-root Kummer map. At every finite Initial Theta core, the completion's canonical discrete valuation is proved compatible with its topology and makes it an MLF; the separable/algebraic closure comparison constructs this embedding on the core's exact local absolute Galois group. The pair is then transported to the arithmetic fundamental-group quotient by the geometric image, where its canonical unit Kummer map is again proved injective. A pointed inversion has an actual decomposition subgroup, and the exact equality M_TM^x intersect res^-1(torsion)=M_TM^mu derives the weaker detection implication and splitting. For both finite mu_2l and infinite mu orbits, the identity representative and finite-order action prove the entire final zero-label orbit is torsion; the composite H1 restriction constructs both zero-label splittings. Constructing the restricted-tempered map to this local MLF quotient and its coefficient comparison, proving the pointed inverse-image equality from Corollary 1.12, and identifying the two-stage composite with that pointed restriction remain open.",
